Energy behavior

Charged BA1 still costs exactly 25 Energy once per accepted summon.

Do not introduce a second charge.

The overhead fallback is not a different player action and does not cost additional Energy.

It is simply the alternate execution of the same paid ba1Clone summon.

Maintain the existing guarantee that missing required art/data does not consume Energy for an invisible/broken summon.

Because Fighter.trySummon() currently runs summonProblem() before spending Energy, extend validation appropriately for the optional no-ground attack.

For #0001, both:

ba1
midairBa2

must have valid definitions, hitboxes and animation frames before this summon is considered fully usable.

Do not create location-dependent energy loss where Energy is paid and then Clone.summon() silently fails because the fallback attack is unavailable.

summonProblem()

Update summonProblem() generically.

It currently validates:

* cloud;
* def.attack;
* attack hitbox;
* attack animation frames.

When a summon declares a noGround/fallback attack, validate that attack as well.

Avoid #0001-specific strings.

A helper for validating an attack ID would be appropriate.

For example conceptually:

validateSummonAttack(owner, attackId)

called for the primary attack and optional no-ground attack.

Existing summon definitions without a no-ground fallback must continue to work exactly as before.

Stage bounds

Keep the current stageMargin behavior.

Normal behind X must continue to be clamped.

Overhead X must also be kept within the stage margins, although target.body.x will normally already be valid.

Ground detection must happen using the final clamped normal behind X, because that is where the clone would actually spawn.

Do not test support at an unclamped off-stage coordinate and then spawn somewhere else.

Tests

Expand tests/clone.test.mjs substantially.

Do not remove the existing clone coverage.

First fix the test harness

In tests/fighter-harness.mjs, duel() accepts a custom stage, but the clone spawn call currently uses the global STAGE:

