Definition of done

The implementation is complete when all of the following are true:

1. Charged BA1 on normal ground behaves exactly as it does now.
2. A clone behind an opponent remains BA1 whenever that behind position has support at the opponent’s current foot level.
3. If that position has no same-height support, the clone instead appears above the opponent.
4. The overhead clone plays the existing five-frame midairBa2.
5. Its real existing hitbox naturally connects with a stationary target.
6. A hit does 6 damage and applies existing High reversed vertical Knockback, driving the target downward.
7. It is still a detached clone hit credited to #0001.
8. The clone remains stationary/non-physical and does not track.
9. Cloud appearance and disappearance remain unchanged.
10. Energy cost remains 25.
11. Missing required fallback art/data cannot consume Energy for a broken summon.
12. Stage-edge behavior remains correct.
13. The implementation is generic/data-driven, with no 0001 or midairBa2 special case inside the clone engine.
14. Existing tests pass and new regression tests cover the platform-edge and airborne cases.
15. ALVA_SPEC.md accurately describes the final behavior.

